{
  "case_id": "2010-10-188",
  "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: STEVEN ALAN REISS, ESQ., New York, New York; on behalf of Petitioner. JONATHAN A. WILLENS, ESQ., New York, New York; on behalf of Respondent. MELISSA ARBUS SHERRY, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But suppose the FOIA information is just to confirm, to back up, to fill out;"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Schindler Elevator Corporation",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "district court did in this very case in a very thorough opinion. Judge Stein went through every element required for the public disclosure bar to be invoked, including whether the FOIA response was a report or investigation, including whether Mr. Kirk's complaint was based on allegations and transactions disclosed in that FOIA response, and concluded that every prong of the disclosure -- public disclosure bar was met, and, therefore, the public disclosure bar prevented Mr. Kirk's claims. And that is precisely the analysis that we contend ought to happen."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Give us -- give us your definition. You say you're not standing by the dictionary definition -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Willens",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's the Second Circuit's holding, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Which is -- can you point us to the page so we can see the Second Circuit's definition of report and the Second Circuit's definition of an FCA investigation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if we adopt your definition, isn't it true that a lot of things that are labeled Department of Labor report, Justice Department Freedom of Information Act report, are not reports?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, the -- I think you've just divided up two issues. The first is, the FOIA letter does tell you that there weren't reports for certain years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Willens",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The plain language of FOIA indicates that a response is not a report; a search is not an investigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Melissa Arbus Sherry",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0001-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I want to start with one thing that hasn't yet been brought up this morning, and that is the context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: No, no, it says, please tell me any documents that they filed that says da, da, da, something like that, okay? Now, we have the same thing, word for word, except the person who makes the request is not Mrs. Mary Jones from the public, the person who makes the request is the fraud officer for the agency that's worried about being defrauded."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government (Ms. Sherry)",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SHERRY: In the Government's view the fact that the information was obtained through a FOIA request doesn't answer the question as to whether the underlying document is an administrative report or an administrative audit or anything else of the sort. The FOIA -- the agency's response to a FOIA request, again, is nothing more than the first -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Did the FCA, the amendments in 2009, which are not retroactive, do they have any bearing on this problem prospectively?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Reiss)",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. REISS: I don't think I'll use it all, Mr. Chief Justice. Justice Ginsburg, in response to your request, the new version of the False Claims Act lets the government disclaim the public disclosure bar. It now says the bar can apply unless opposed by the government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ae27f42c8c5ccf31ecd9269d994d8c87103830d5687d38aaedd81c2c934fe20",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ae27f42c8c5-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. Mr. Reiss, you have 14 minutes remaining."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-10-188",
